    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d815">

                <pb facs="0824" n="706" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg706"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.5712a/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Swenson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-10T16:00:00-05:00">March 10, 1928—4
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1. Department handed Norwegian Minister today a draft of a proposed treaty of
                    arbitration between the United States and Norway.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d815-f1"
                    /> The provisions of the draft operate to extend the policy of arbitration
                    enunciated in the Root Treaty of April 4, 1908.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d815-f2"/>
                    The language of the preamble and of the articles covering arbitration is
                    identical in effect with that employed in the draft arbitration treaties
                    recently submitted to the French, British, Italian and Japanese
                        Governments.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d815-f3"/></p>
                <p>Text of proposed treaty will be forwarded in next pouch.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
